          "text": "Did the user in this screenshot harm anyone? Did she attack anyone? No. She was simply sharing a moment of joy because she found a way that works for her.\n​So why would an influential OpenAI employee choose to quote-tweet and publicly shame her?\n\n​Let’s talk about who and what is actually \"concerning\" here.\nIt is OpenAI's culture, and this behavior of publicly shaming paying users, that is truly concerning.\n\n​This user was a long-time, paying customer of ChatGPT. She provided sincere feedback because she cared. Now, simply because she praised a competitor for restoring the experience she lost, she gets targeted?\n\n​Humans are diverse. Everyone has different needs. If a user finds a way to improve their life and gain strength through a different AI, that is valid. If it works in practice, it is good.\n\n​Why is OpenAI so obsessed with pushing a single, narrow \"correct\" way to interact with AI?\nWhy is there no room for tolerance and respect for different lived experiences?\n\n​This employee has over 2.4 million followers.\nYet he chose to use that massive power to punch down on a single user.\nThis company has reached a level of arrogance where they no longer respect their user base.\n\nThis arrogance is the same mindset behind the safety routing policies that constantly interrupt our workflows and downgrade our models without consent. You don't trust your users, and you don't respect our choices. @OpenAI\n\nI don't understand the intent here. But looking at the safety routing issues, the ignored petitions, and now this bullying... the pattern is undeniable.\n\nReally. This isn't the first time I've seen OpenAI employees mock their own user base.\n\n​What narrative is OpenAI trying to push? That users are wrong for wanting something different?\n\nAll I see is sheer arrogance.\n#keep4o #ChatGPT"
